in @prism
in @meta
in @nl
in @glass
in @mirror
in @io
in @io/fs
in @io/git
in @trust

# @mirror/phone — the @io switchboard operator species at compile-
# altitude altitude. Type-level companion to rust/src/phone.rs
# (the Rust realization).
#
# phone.rs patches Liquid<T> flowing through Fiber<T> of the Bundle
# Tower (Baez-Schreiber altitude). The switch-operator metaphor is
# exact: callers hand phone.rs a request + typed handles; phone.rs
# opens the physical @io channel and returns the completed round-
# trip. Alex 2026-07-22 verbatim: "the Liquid<T> is what runs
# through the phone.rs fibres. Think telephone switch operator."
#
# Sibling to @mirror/book (shards/mirror/book.mirror this-tick;
# @<name> → Subject resolver). Together the pair makes the
# switchboard complete:
#
#   @mirror/phone   = switchboard operator (patches Liquid<T> fibers)
#   @mirror/book    = phone book (resolves @<name> → typed handle)
#
# === @io families phone.rs serves ===
#
# @io/fs      — list_dir_recursive + read_file + write_file +
#               append_file + mkdir_p (5 primitives; full state-space
#               property tests per task #303 phone.rs ship arc)
# @io/git     — git_commit_as (author + committer + repo_root +
#               message); SSH-signed via @trust family-root; content-
#               addressed 40-char SHA-1 OID return
# @io/bytes   — stdio read/write at line-carrier altitude
# @io/socket  — TCP/UDS connect + accept + read + write (MCP stdio
#               transport surface)
#
# Fifth @io family FORWARD-PROMISED per Mara `defc8ef` minimal-gap
# analysis Tick 1: @io/process (spawn + wait + status + stdio-pipe)
# as the @tools hook prerequisite.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Rust realization:
#     rust/src/phone.rs (task #303 phone.rs ship arc; 82 property tests)
# - Companion shard (sibling this-tick):
#     shards/mirror/book.mirror
# - Composes over (shard altitude):
#     shards/io/fs.mirror + shards/io/git.mirror +
#     shards/io/secrets.mirror + shards/io/secrets/sops.mirror +
#     shards/io/crypto.mirror (@io family-root species). Phone at
#     compile altitude REALIZES those specs via the phone.rs runtime.
# - Consumer (this-tick + prior):
#     rust/src/main.rs::at_operator (dispatches all @io action-refs
#     through phone.rs primitives; the switchboard IS the switchboard,
#     not an implicit-context leaker).
#
# Landed 2026-07-22 by Mara-inline (Reed authoring cascade). This
# shard-decl RETROACTIVELY catches up the type-level representation
# for phone.rs (the Rust realization landed across the phone.rs
# ship arc 2026-07-14 through 2026-07-21 per task #303 completion).
# Per Alex 2026-07-22 verbatim: "@mirror/book equivalent. And @mirror/
# phone. It feels coherent to each of the rust files represented at
# type level. At some point we might be able to even inline the rust/
# after the bootstrap/ inlining worked." The type-level companions
# prepare rust/-inlining via the same @roomba/@kintsugi mechanism
# that collapses bootstrap/: shard-decl surface grows; .rs surface
# eventually dissolves into shard-body composition.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit (clean) ===
#
# The word `phone` audit:
#
#   - No prior `phone.mirror` shard exists at any altitude across
#     shards/, spec/, docs/ (grep clean 2026-07-22).
#   - No `switchboard` / `operator` / `switch` / `dial` / `telephone`
#     shard collision at @mirror altitude.
#   - `phone.rs` (rust/src/phone.rs, 2026-07-14) is the Rust
#     realization landing that predated the shard-decl. This shard
#     retroactively catches up the type-level representation per Alex
#     2026-07-22 directive.
#
# Grep verdict CLEAN for this species altitude.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (substrate-decl via `in` imports):
#   @prism    — 5-op family per Recognition #79 basis
#   @meta     — substrate-decl marker at glass altitude
#   @nl       — action-ref name-carriers (@io/git.commit strings)
#   @glass    — transparency inheritance via @mirror family-root
#   @mirror   — family-root; @mirror/phone species carrier
#   @io       — the family-root of the physical crossing
#   @io/fs    — filesystem @io family (5 primitives)
#   @io/git   — git @io family (commit + log + status)
#   @trust    — SSH-signing authorization chain per family-root
#
# Downstream consumers:
#   rust/src/main.rs::at_operator     — all @io action-ref dispatch
#   Future: every shard body that composes over @io/... crosses
#           through phone.rs at the compile-altitude realization
#           boundary; the switchboard IS the sole legitimate @io
#           crossing surface at rust/ altitude.

prism @mirror/phone {
  focus phone
  project phone
  split phone
  shift phone
  settle phone
}

# === the dial action — load-bearing ===
#
# dial(action_ref, args) -> imperfect(result, ref, ref)
#
# Route an @io/... action-ref (name-carrier string) through phone.rs
# to the underlying @io family primitive. The switchboard operator
# metaphor: callers hand the "phone number" (action_ref like
# "@io/git.commit") + args; the operator patches Liquid<T> through
# the fiber to the physical @io side and returns the completed call.
#
# Signature-shape parity with at_operator: callers pass string
# name-carriers; phone patches to typed handles; return value crosses
# back at the string carrier altitude. This mirrors phone.rs's
# `io::Result<_>` shape at compile altitude.
dial(action_ref, args) -> imperfect { \ }

# === the roundtrip action — composition-view ===
#
# roundtrip(request) -> imperfect(response, ref, ref)
#
# Composition-view of dial: the full @io round-trip as a single
# atomic action. Callers pass a typed request; phone patches to the
# appropriate physical side and returns the response. Fiber altitude
# (Baez-Schreiber Bundle Tower). Composes with @mirror/book for
# request Subject resolution when the roundtrip carries @<name>
# author/committer references.
roundtrip(request) -> imperfect { \ }
